So first off, what is
shiny by definition

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:48.020
is a framework that allows R
users to create interactive web

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:51.260
apps without knowing
anything about web design.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.750
So you don't really have to
think about all the underlying

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.730
web technologies you just use.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:03:00.120
And it's kind of similar
to learning a new package.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:01.000
They're a little bit.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.917
You don't really need
to know basis webdesign,

00:03:02.917 --> 00:03:07.170
but just a few basic
things is helpful.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:10.180
So here's the one slide that
I'm going to talk about.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.710
Web design, as I said,
abstracts away the underlying

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.980
technologies of the web design.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.350
Which are three of them?

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.480
There's TML, which I'm
sure sounds probably

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.010
sounds pretty familiar if you
haven't worked with it before.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.400
It's essentially the
building block of a web page

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.870
and your web browser
interprets it

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.390
and shows you the nice
reformatted websites that

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:35.820
were all used to their success
or cascading style sheets.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.850
And this separates the content.

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:43.320
It's in what your app is
doing or what your website

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.235
is doing with how it looks.

00:03:45.235 --> 00:03:46.860
So you can control
those independently,

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:49.925
you can change the content,
or you can update the theme.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.120
But they're not tied together.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.380
They're independent.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.060
And then finally,
there's Javascript,

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:00.600
which is scripting language
that enables the interactivity

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.060
within a web page or a web app.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.790
And typically, this is
executed in the user's browser

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:08.280
rather than on any
central server.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.670
And the idea with shinee is
that it takes all of this

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:15.160
and wraps it up into an easy
to use interface and framework.

